====== Leetcode 75. Sort Colors (27th Feb)=======
Algorithm for sorting 0s, 1s, and 2s (Dutch National Flag method):
Step 1: Initialize three pointers:
•	st at the beginning (index 0)
•	mid at the beginning (index 0)
•	end at the last index of the array
Step 2: Repeat the following steps while mid is less than or equal to end.
Step 3: If the value at mid is 1,
move mid one step forward.
Step 4: If the value at mid is 0,
swap the value at st and mid using the swap method,
then move both st and mid one step forward.
Step 5: If the value at mid is 2,
swap the value at mid and end using the swap method,
then move end one step backward.
Do not move mid in this case.
Step 6: Continue this process until mid becomes greater than end.
Step 7: When the loop ends, the array will be sorted with all 0s first, then 1s, then 2s. 
Time Complexity = O(n) 
Space Complexity = O(1)


          ----------------> Code <--------------------
class Solution {
    public void sortColors(int[] nums) {
        int st=0,mid=0,end=nums.length-1;
        while(mid<=end){
            if(nums[mid]==1){
                mid++;
            }else if(nums[mid]==0){
                if(st!=mid)swap(nums,st,mid);
                mid++;
                st++;
            }else{
                swap(nums,mid,end);
                end--;
            }
        }
    }
    public void swap(int[] nums,int a,int b){
        int temp=nums[a];
        nums[a]=nums[b];
        nums[b]=temp;
    }
}
